%% DM26-0670

%% What the broker does about a subscriber that falls behind, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-backpressure.md, "The stall
%% rule ends only a subscriber that makes no progress", and cassini-broker.md "The bounds, as built"). A slow subscriber that keeps
%% acknowledging holds its topic back and is never ended. Only a connection that acknowledges nothing for the stall bound is.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Slow client
    participant Listener as its Listener and reader
    participant Sub as SubscriberAgent
    participant Topic as TopicAgent
    participant Pub as Publisher
    participant Pressure as PressureManager
    participant Session as its SessionAgent
    participant SM as SessionManager

    Sub->>Listener: PushMessage(delivery_id), kept in the delivery outbox until acknowledged
    Note over Sub: Its backlog is what is delivered and not acknowledged. Its high water is an eighth<br/>of the budget as it is now, never under 1 MiB, with hysteresis down to half of it.
    opt above its high water, and connected
        Sub->>Topic: TopicHold(holding): to the ref the topic gave it (TopicAttached)
        Topic->>Topic: accepts no publish: they wait in order, each holding its connection's window
        Topic--xPub: no acknowledgement comes, so the publisher's credit runs out and it slows
    end
    Client->>Listener: PublishResponseAck(delivery_id)
    Listener->>Session: ConnectionProgress, told by the reader, beside the Listener's mailbox
    Listener->>Sub: PublishResponseAck, and its backlog falls
    opt below half its high water
        Sub->>Topic: TopicHold(not holding): the topic pumps what waits
    end

    Note over Pressure,Sub: A stall check is a quarter of the stall bound, between 50 ms and 5 s, and the bound is 30 s by default.
    alt the budget is exhausted
        Pressure->>Sub: BudgetExhausted, through the SubscriberManager
        Sub->>Sub: a client that is away lets go of what it held (shed_if_away: broker/client_disconnect)
    else it is not
        Pressure->>Sub: StallCheck, through the SubscriberManager
    end
    opt above its high water for the bound, or, the budget exhausted, nothing acknowledged for the bound
        Note over Sub: The clock counts only time spent connected.
        Sub->>Session: SubscriberStalled(topic, held, stalled_for)
        Session->>Session: pressure::verdict, from what it knows of its connection
        alt it read an acknowledgement on any topic within the bound, or was spared within it
            Session->>Session: Ignore: slow is not stalled, and any condemnation is forgotten
        else its reader waits for admission, and it has made progress since it was last spared
            Session->>Listener: refuse_for(the bound): Spare, so its reader refuses for now and reads on
            Note over Session,Listener: What it acknowledged may be unread behind that wait, so it is not ended for it.
        else nothing acknowledged, nothing to spare it for
            Session->>Session: Condemn, and look again an eighth of the bound on
            opt still so at a later look
                Session->>Listener: cut, from outside the Listener, which may be waiting on a write to this client
                Listener--xClient: the connection ends
                Session->>SM: SessionStallEnded: logged with the identity, the topic, the bytes and how long
                Listener->>SM: DisconnectRequest: the session detaches for the retention window
                Note over Topic,SM: The topic moves again, and the client may come back and be sent what it is owed.
            end
        end
    end
